      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design the Proximity Service",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design the Proximity Service",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hoYbwDGvYiueeGSLOtq1G",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12422.435261448456,
      "y": -1672.356928694111,
      "width": 672.259521484375,
      "height": 1475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 735636982,
      "version": 1288,
      "versionNonce": 1500853174,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752081454476,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional requirements: \n    - Near by restaurents.\n    - with their location.\n    - register restaurent. \n    \n\nNon functional requirements:\n    - its okk, not need immediate restaurent\n      to be reflected. \n    - high search qps.\n    - high scalable and available.\n    - can limit upto which find restaurent. \n      let say under 10km only.  \n    \nEstimations:\n    - qps write -> 1k  / s\n    - read : write -> 100:1\n    -> 100k / s -> read near by restaurent.\n    -> storage -> 5 years -> \n        -> per second -> 100b per row.\n        -> per second -> 100kb \n        -> per day -> ~ 10 GB\n        -> per year -> ~4 tb\n        -> 5 year -> 20 tb -> its ok to be in a single node. \n    \nEntities:\n    - restaurent, restaurentLocation.\n\nApi design: \n\n    - /api/v1/proximity/register       POST\n    \n    x-token, x-trace-id\n    \n    Request: { restaurent, location }\n    Response: { success }\n    \n    - /api/v1/proximity/?lat=<>&&long=<>&&pageSize&&offset=<> get\n    \n    paginated\n    \n    Response: { pagesize, offset, resaurents: [{restaurent}] }\n    \n\nDb schema: \n\n- Restaurents:\n    - id\n    - name\n    - address\n    - ..\n- Restaurent Location\n    - id\n    - restaurentId\n    - long\n    - lat\n\nlater .. \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional requirements: \n    - Near by restaurents.\n    - with their location.\n    - register restaurent. \n    \n\nNon functional requirements:\n    - its okk, not need immediate restaurent\n      to be reflected. \n    - high search qps.\n    - high scalable and available.\n    - can limit upto which find restaurent. \n      let say under 10km only.  \n    \nEstimations:\n    - qps write -> 1k  / s\n    - read : write -> 100:1\n    -> 100k / s -> read near by restaurent.\n    -> storage -> 5 years -> \n        -> per second -> 100b per row.\n        -> per second -> 100kb \n        -> per day -> ~ 10 GB\n        -> per year -> ~4 tb\n        -> 5 year -> 20 tb -> its ok to be in a single node. \n    \nEntities:\n    - restaurent, restaurentLocation.\n\nApi design: \n\n    - /api/v1/proximity/register       POST\n    \n    x-token, x-trace-id\n    \n    Request: { restaurent, location }\n    Response: { success }\n    \n    - /api/v1/proximity/?lat=<>&&long=<>&&pageSize&&offset=<> get\n    \n    paginated\n    \n    Response: { pagesize, offset, resaurents: [{restaurent}] }\n    \n\nDb schema: \n\n- Restaurents:\n    - id\n    - name\n    - address\n    - ..\n- Restaurent Location\n    - id\n    - restaurentId\n    - long\n    - lat\n\nlater .. \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
