    {
      "id": "KsLivYkv8J-0HN-dODHjj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13335.39946206838,
      "y": -991.2921468198706,
      "width": 913.0394287109375,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1996712938,
      "version": 2033,
      "versionNonce": 694910454,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752090761623,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solutions: \n\n1.  Simple with help of finding the distance in long and lat\n    using sql query.\n\n    with index on long and lat.\n\n    write per second is ok 1k , but if increase then can cause issue.\n   \n    100k/qps is too high for read. and also read query\n    is bit complext basically for all restaurent check the distance between their \n    location.\n\n   usually mysql read took single to double digit in micro second -> here it can go upto 3 digit\n   like 100ms -> 0.1 second -> \n  \n  Some solution\n        - partition data with region since nearby is about region.\n        - multiple table as per region.\n        - that wil reduce size and search \n\n     \n  redis to save -> how ? -> \n        - not efficient to save with lat and long.\n        - may be with help of local area like pincode etc. \n\n  that can help to bit better.\n\n  But we can more better solution. Now a days.   \n    \n    \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solutions: \n\n1.  Simple with help of finding the distance in long and lat\n    using sql query.\n\n    with index on long and lat.\n\n    write per second is ok 1k , but if increase then can cause issue.\n   \n    100k/qps is too high for read. and also read query\n    is bit complext basically for all restaurent check the distance between their \n    location.\n\n   usually mysql read took single to double digit in micro second -> here it can go upto 3 digit\n   like 100ms -> 0.1 second -> \n  \n  Some solution\n        - partition data with region since nearby is about region.\n        - multiple table as per region.\n        - that wil reduce size and search \n\n     \n  redis to save -> how ? -> \n        - not efficient to save with lat and long.\n        - may be with help of local area like pincode etc. \n\n  that can help to bit better.\n\n  But we can more better solution. Now a days.   \n    \n    \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
