    {
      "id": "89fWfY7FQBYK-5CzofuGI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14396.490285736953,
      "y": -937.1352368344604,
      "width": 765.0594482421875,
      "height": 1250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1732245430,
      "version": 826,
      "versionNonce": 450373110,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752090761623,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2.  We do have google maps we are change this 3d map to 2d map \n    to unique id for each partition\n\n    break down map into 4 section, then its 4 second.\n    basically this is called gecoding. \n\n    won't go in deep dive.\n    \n    baiscally we can change whole 2d map into smaller box with having unique id\n    this box length depend up how many times divide. \n    \n    \n    so we can as per our near length we can divide and whenever location \n    comes we can assign it a that geohash with one more depth. \n    \n    \n    now we can search all restaurent with perfix match quer. \n    \n    like location.  01010110\n    \n    then all location like \"0101011%\"\n    \n    How to create this hash -> see nearby HLD.\n\n    Problem: Boundary Condition: \n\n    To soalve this we can find the near all 8 geohashh and find all\n     restaurent there. -> more detail -> nearby HLD\n\n\n    for this can use redis to do this. \n\n    and geoindex postgres\n\n    redis also support near by with geohash \n\n     Problem 2: not restauranet in just near by geohash\n     then increase more boundary. \n\n\n\n     Database: \n\n     restaurentId, geohash, createdTime. \n     \n\n     Cache: -> redis have geohash already, just register it. \n\n     \n      cache 2: geohash: { list of restaurents }",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2.  We do have google maps we are change this 3d map to 2d map \n    to unique id for each partition\n\n    break down map into 4 section, then its 4 second.\n    basically this is called gecoding. \n\n    won't go in deep dive.\n    \n    baiscally we can change whole 2d map into smaller box with having unique id\n    this box length depend up how many times divide. \n    \n    \n    so we can as per our near length we can divide and whenever location \n    comes we can assign it a that geohash with one more depth. \n    \n    \n    now we can search all restaurent with perfix match quer. \n    \n    like location.  01010110\n    \n    then all location like \"0101011%\"\n    \n    How to create this hash -> see nearby HLD.\n\n    Problem: Boundary Condition: \n\n    To soalve this we can find the near all 8 geohashh and find all\n     restaurent there. -> more detail -> nearby HLD\n\n\n    for this can use redis to do this. \n\n    and geoindex postgres\n\n    redis also support near by with geohash \n\n     Problem 2: not restauranet in just near by geohash\n     then increase more boundary. \n\n\n\n     Database: \n\n     restaurentId, geohash, createdTime. \n     \n\n     Cache: -> redis have geohash already, just register it. \n\n     \n      cache 2: geohash: { list of restaurents }",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Q939i-xPuQYP7dUJDhztt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13291.009868761554,
      "y": -156.2789824566903,
      "width": 638.5595092773438,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 539291126,
      "version": 2806,
      "versionNonce": 1541242218,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1752091140522,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " \n\n3.  Since its is ok restaurent update bit later no real time.\n    we can use some data strcture which will divide map \n    in node with having at max 100 restaurents.\n\n    divide the map into 4 if > 100 \n\n     Problem algo check in hands on. \n\n\n   With the help of this , we can make in memory quadtree\n   and at time of start can read from the database.\n   here we don't need the geohash, normal db would be.\n\n\n   and after some internal we can refresh this inmemory database\n   as per our trade off.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " \n\n3.  Since its is ok restaurent update bit later no real time.\n    we can use some data strcture which will divide map \n    in node with having at max 100 restaurents.\n\n    divide the map into 4 if > 100 \n\n     Problem algo check in hands on. \n\n\n   With the help of this , we can make in memory quadtree\n   and at time of start can read from the database.\n   here we don't need the geohash, normal db would be.\n\n\n   and after some internal we can refresh this inmemory database\n   as per our trade off.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xIgwZlE89S_ttT01SHEnt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13311.526704433612,
      "y": 375.4916468114647,
      "width": 860.2994384765625,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 842574570,
      "version": 978,
      "versionNonce": 741897014,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752160285459,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Challenge, \n- would it be able to cache that much data in memoroy ? \n    - total restaurent is not as per 1k/s \n    - we do have 9B user in world :)\n    - lets assume 200M total restaurents.\n    - size: \n    - each note would have lat ( double -> 8byte) and long and 4 pointer ( 8*4 byte)\n    - leaf will have lat long 100 restaurentsid -> ( 100 * 8 byte)\n    - total -> 2M  * 850b + 2M/3 * 50b -> ~2M*1000b -> 2G -> that is ok\n- How would you load from db efficiently\n    -  fetch 2M restaurent batch by batch -> should be able to complete in few minutes.\n- Updation.\n    - maintain the trigger peiorically ( depending upon criticality) , \n     that will fetch new restaurents  and insert into quadtree\n    - in book its next day, dynamic updating bit complex single we'll have to make sure\n     about consistency and locking ,by multpoe thread.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Challenge, \n- would it be able to cache that much data in memoroy ? \n    - total restaurent is not as per 1k/s \n    - we do have 9B user in world :)\n    - lets assume 200M total restaurents.\n    - size: \n    - each note would have lat ( double -> 8byte) and long and 4 pointer ( 8*4 byte)\n    - leaf will have lat long 100 restaurentsid -> ( 100 * 8 byte)\n    - total -> 2M  * 850b + 2M/3 * 50b -> ~2M*1000b -> 2G -> that is ok\n- How would you load from db efficiently\n    -  fetch 2M restaurent batch by batch -> should be able to complete in few minutes.\n- Updation.\n    - maintain the trigger peiorically ( depending upon criticality) , \n     that will fetch new restaurents  and insert into quadtree\n    - in book its next day, dynamic updating bit complex single we'll have to make sure\n     about consistency and locking ,by multpoe thread.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
